      'MODEL (R4-11): Opus 4.6 on Bedrock (global.anthropic.claude-opus-4-6-v1) everywhere the narrative is written; provider + model stamped on every stored narrative and read back off the trace (DEC-2 — a disagreement is a refusal). MEASURED live 18 Aug: 22–25 s per call (2.9–4.2k in / ~1.1k out, ~$0.05), citations valid 4/4 → inline by default within the ≤ 80 s leg budget; worker box redone (≈ 790,000 of 800,000 ms by the 200 s-per-leg worst case; the leg runs after saveAuditResult so an overrun never costs a finding).',
      'BACKFILL (R4-8): worker \'readmission\' on the SAME backfill_runs rails — Bedrock-only (typed), the exact Opus id enforced, n_per_tick clamped ≤ 2, cursor over audited_at UTC days (empty days marched past inside a tick), fill-only predicate "audited AND no caseNarrative", per-run tokens/cost, §C4 stop-race writes, reachability re-checked every tick, progress surface (pace / ETA / stall / backlog) on the runner\'s GET. Ticks come from the existing every-2-minutes OPD backfill cron when the OPD worker is idle (vercel.json untouched) and from ?auto=1. Never auto-started: an operator POSTs start_run. Backlog at build: 54 audited findings at readmission/0.2 (the R2 refill is still filling toward ~135).',
      'STALE-ID FILTER (Addendum A1, the backfill blocker): on the REBUILT-ledger path every stored audit-time evidence id fed to the prompt (omission evidenceIds, exculpatory corroboratingIds, id-shaped mentions in the weakest step / refusal notes / claims) is filtered to ids the rebuilt ledger carries BEFORE the model sees it, and the count is stored as staleIdsDropped on the narrative — closing the one path where a citation could be valid-by-code yet point at the wrong item. Inline path unchanged (its ledger IS the audit\'s). Worker max is clamped to conc (Addendum A3): a second wave cannot fit the box, so ?max=10 is unfireable.',
