      'THE TWO STORED JUDGEMENTS (§4, verbatim): preventable injury — any high-danger omission → suspected; else a moderate omission matching a clinical-harm stem (wound · infect · bleed · sepsis · dehisc · implant fail · intra-?op · unstable · \\bSSI\\b) → suspected; else zero omissions AND lab-corroborated AND stability corroborated → not_suggested; else unknown. Negligence — suspected ONLY when planned=unplanned AND sameCondition ≠ different AND an omission matches an intra-op/peri-op EVENT pattern (intra-?op · intraoperative · operative finding · calcar · cerclage · anastomot · retained · wrong[- ]site); zero omissions + lab-corroborated + stability corroborated → not_suggested; else unknown. Medical justification is a display mapping of the stored money verdict (justified / needs_adjudication / avoidable→Not justified / null→Needs adjudication), not stored.',
