      'VERSIONED BACKFILL: the migrate route selects audited rows WHERE preventable_injury IS NULL OR negligence IS NULL OR judgement_rule_version IS DISTINCT FROM the current constant, re-derives from the `finding` jsonb in JS, and stamps the version — ≤200 rows per request, safe to re-run, returns scanned/updated/remaining. A future rule change bumps JUDGEMENT_RULE_VERSION and the same step re-derives everything. The migration is written here and RUNS AT SHIP TIME after V\'s GO; until it runs, the list read (which now selects the three columns) soft-fails to an empty board, so migrate BEFORE the deploy is exercised.',
