    why: 'The judge that decides whether a clinician sees a low-value-care flag was disagreeing with itself once in every five notes, and a 14B model on an office machine was quietly allowed to be the one answering. Determinism was the cheap half; the honest half was ruling that when the right model cannot answer, the system says nothing rather than something.',
