      '§2.3 STANDS: a terminal empty-200 still throws the marked ProviderResponseError and still refuses the Ollama fallback. The retry budget changes WHEN it throws, never what happens after. Streaming calls keep the bare SDK call — an in-flight stream must not be aborted by a wall-clock timer.',
      'TASK 2 SAFETY: a successful row is never overwritten (the WHERE excludes it — a plain save still returns \'exists\'); the experiment cohort is untouchable (its filter admits only excluded_reason IS NULL or vertex_outage_mislabel_2026_07, and no llm_leg_failed row is ever in it); audited_at moves only on rows no read surface counts. Force mode is unchanged and remains banned for this recovery (it overwrites successful rows and re-stamps their audited_at).',
