    engine: '0.81.17', date: '2026-07-29', scoring: true,
    plain: 'Vitamin D results are now read against a ratified table instead of the model\'s memory. Two notes from the same prescriber on the same day — 17 and 18 ng/mL, with identical treatment courses — had scored 100 and 60. One nanogram, forty points. The engine turned out to hold no vitamin D threshold at all: the cutoff was the model\'s recall, and it was attributed in the written rationale to guidelines that exist nowhere in this system. A published band table now decides deficient, insufficient and sufficient, with no undefined gap between them. Where the treatment matches the result, the audit stays silent; where a recheck should be written down, it asks for one — and that ask never lowers a score.',
